---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Why cnjianghu exists, what it publishes, and how it approaches cultural explanation."
>
  <div class="container-wide py-12 md:py-20">
    <header class="grid gap-10 border-b border-ink-200 pb-12 dark:border-ink-800 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.45fr)_minmax(17rem,0.55fr)] lg:items-end">
      <div class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="mb-5 font-ui text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-vermilion">
          Independent editorial project
        </p>
        <h1 class="max-w-3xl text-5xl font-bold leading-[0.98] text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-50 md:text-7xl">
          A bridge,<br />not a brochure.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
          cnjianghu explains the China people encounter in ordinary life, online culture,
          aesthetics, language, and technology—without flattening it into headlines,
          slogans, or “fun facts.”
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="border-l-2 border-vermilion pl-5 font-ui text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
        <p class="font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">
          江湖 <span class="font-normal italic text-ink-500">(jiāng hú)</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Literally “rivers and lakes”: the living world beneath formal structures,
          where culture is practiced, negotiated, remixed, and passed on.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <main class="mt-14 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-16 lg:grid-cols-[13rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
      <div class="font-ui text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-500">
        Why it exists
      </div>
      <section class="prose m-0">
        <p>
          Global interest in China is growing, but good context remains hard to find.
          The most useful Chinese-language material is scattered across platforms;
          English-language coverage often lands at one of two extremes—too thin to explain
          much, or too academic to enter easily.
        </p>
        <p>
          cnjianghu works in the space between them. It uses stories, scenes, Chinese terms,
          and visible sources to help curious readers understand not only what something is,
          but why it makes sense from inside its cultural setting.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="font-ui text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-500">
        What it is—and is not
      </div>
      <section class="grid gap-8 border-y border-ink-200 py-9 dark:border-ink-800 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-50">It is</h2>
          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
            <li>Curated cultural explanation for an English-speaking reader.</li>
            <li>An archive of connected stories, concepts, and everyday details.</li>
            <li>An invitation to stay curious when a simple analogy stops working.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-50">It is not</h2>
          <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
            <li>A news outlet, tourism guide, or substitute for scholarship.</li>
            <li>A claim that there is one universal “Chinese perspective.”</li>
            <li>A polished national image that removes contradiction or change.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="font-ui text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-500">
        Editorial principles
      </div>
      <section>
        <ol class="divide-y divide-ink-200 border-y border-ink-200 dark:divide-ink-800 dark:border-ink-800">
          {
            [
              ['01', 'Context before conclusion', 'Explain the social setting and competing interpretations before reducing a subject to one takeaway.'],
              ['02', 'Specific before sweeping', 'Use a scene, object, word, or documented example instead of speaking for 1.4 billion people.'],
              ['03', 'Sources before confidence', 'Treat links as evidence to inspect, not decoration added after the writing is finished.'],
              ['04', 'Curiosity before performance', 'The goal is understanding—not defending, attacking, or turning complexity into a spectacle.'],
            ].map(([number, title, body]) => (
              <li class="grid gap-3 py-6 md:grid-cols-[3.5rem_14rem_minmax(0,1fr)] md:items-baseline">
                <span class="font-ui text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] text-vermilion">{number}</span>
                <strong class="font-heading text-xl text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-50">{title}</strong>
                <span class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">{body}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </section>

      <div class="font-ui text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-400 dark:text-ink-500">
        Who makes it
      </div>
      <section class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-200">
          cnjianghu is an independently created and edited, open-source cultural project.
          AI tools assist parts of research organization, translation drafting, editing,
          and production. AI output is never treated as a source, and responsibility for
          what appears on the site remains with the project.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 font-ui text-sm">
          <a href="/editorial-standards" class="font-semibold text-vermilion hover:underline">
            Read the editorial standards →
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/Mocooa/cnjianghu"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-ink-600 hover:text-vermilion dark:text-ink-300"
          >
            View the open-source project
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
